WEBVTT

00:21.290 --> 00:23.120
Thank you, Nico!

00:23.120 --> 00:25.750
I'd always dreamed
of taking pictures from the sky.

00:25.750 --> 00:28.630
I'm so glad I have a witch
at my school.

00:28.630 --> 00:31.130
It makes me happy to hear you say that.

00:31.460 --> 00:33.130
See you later, Nico!

00:33.130 --> 00:34.550
Yeah, see ya!

00:36.470 --> 00:38.350
Your magic stone
has been changing color, huh?

00:38.350 --> 00:40.390
Yep, it's all going smoothly.

00:41.140 --> 00:41.890
Watch out!

00:45.390 --> 00:47.520
<i>A rose? Is it a witch?</i>

00:47.520 --> 00:48.650
Who's there?

00:51.820 --> 00:54.030
It's the Student Council.

00:54.030 --> 00:56.030
- You're kidding, right?
- Student Council?

00:56.030 --> 00:58.120
You're dressed so indecently, though!

00:58.200 --> 01:01.370
Oh my, are you blushing?
Such a cute boy.

01:01.370 --> 01:05.710
H-Hey! Moi is an innocent young man,
so please don't touch his chin like that!

01:06.040 --> 01:09.080
What do you want? It's dangerous
throwing around roses like that.

01:09.290 --> 01:12.000
Oh please, that rose is harmless.

01:12.000 --> 01:13.960
It stabbed through concrete.

01:15.170 --> 01:18.970
I'm here to see you, Nico Wakatsuki.

01:19.430 --> 01:22.520
Since your magic could be
a danger to the students, a rule

01:22.520 --> 01:25.680
has been established that prohibits you
from using it at this school.

01:25.680 --> 01:28.020
I just came here to tell you that.

01:28.350 --> 01:30.110
I can't use my magic?

01:30.110 --> 01:31.110
That's oppression!

01:31.110 --> 01:35.070
Establishing such a rule is ridiculous.
We're against it and won't obey it.

01:35.070 --> 01:38.360
Oh wow, look at you,
getting all worked up. Such a cutie.

01:39.990 --> 01:43.120
I'm Ibara Ibu, the vice president.

01:43.410 --> 01:45.250
Really sorry that I scared you.

01:46.960 --> 01:50.250
I'm pleased to meet you,
my little cuties.

01:52.250 --> 01:55.920
<i>This person's character is so tropey.</i>

03:27.560 --> 03:33.520
TROPE-TACULAR STUDENT COUNCIL

03:27.850 --> 03:29.930
Come to think of it, I did hear a rumor.

03:30.390 --> 03:33.520
The newly appointed Student Council
members are all trope-tacular.

03:33.650 --> 03:34.440
Trope-tacular?

03:34.690 --> 03:37.190
Like the tropes that appear in anime a lot.

03:38.650 --> 03:40.240
- Silence, you!
- You're a trope!

03:40.240 --> 03:43.320
You're the sexy, older sister, and you
throw roses and say, "Silence, you!"

03:43.570 --> 03:46.740
Well that's rude of you.
Who're you calling a trope?

03:46.740 --> 03:50.000
The rest of the Council members
are all upset about that rumor.

03:50.000 --> 03:51.710
Then let's see the rest of them.

03:51.910 --> 03:53.830
I'll decide if they're a trope or not.

03:53.830 --> 03:55.790
They're probably
hiding around here, right?

03:57.420 --> 03:59.630
Aww, I got busted, huh?

03:59.630 --> 04:02.840
As expected of you, Otogi.
You're amazing.

04:02.930 --> 04:06.010
First up, we have the other vice president.

04:06.010 --> 04:08.930
Ranking number one as the man
who will most likely betray you,

04:08.930 --> 04:12.390
it's the Kansai-accent, closed-eyes
wise-guy, Yuzuru Kenmochi.

04:09.220 --> 04:13.230
KANSAI-ACCENT,
CLOSED-EYES, WISE-GUY
YUZURU KENMOCHI

04:12.390 --> 04:13.230
Trope!

04:13.440 --> 04:15.600
It's your usual, competent character.

04:15.600 --> 04:18.730
That's pretty rude of you,
as I'm no trope.

04:18.940 --> 04:22.780
He's all smiley and oblivious, but he's
seeping with strong character vibes.

04:23.070 --> 04:25.820
You don't have to say
such strange things.

04:26.160 --> 04:27.910
Girls with good sense get hurt, you know?

04:27.910 --> 04:29.990
He opens his eyes
only when it's important!

04:30.160 --> 04:31.620
Don't get the wrong idea.

04:32.450 --> 04:34.710
It's not like we've been
observing you or anything.

04:35.000 --> 04:37.420
Moving on, we have the two secretaries.

04:37.420 --> 04:39.380
A European-style lolita tsundere

04:39.380 --> 04:41.960
and a Japanese-style horror
cool-dere who are twin sisters.

04:41.960 --> 04:43.420
Syrup and Kuromitsu!

04:41.960 --> 04:45.090
EUROPEAN-LOLI AND WA-LOLI
SYRUP AND KUROMITSU

04:43.420 --> 04:45.090
Lots of descriptions, but still a trope!

04:45.300 --> 04:47.640
When the nue cries, the ogre dies.

04:47.640 --> 04:49.720
The Japanese-style said something.
Trope!

04:50.060 --> 04:53.600
Well, if you really want to get to know me,
I guess that's fine.

04:53.600 --> 04:54.730
Giving in already?

04:54.730 --> 04:56.770
You guys are just
a bunch of trope characters!

04:56.980 --> 04:59.690
<i>Well, I don't think I'm a trope.</i>

05:00.570 --> 05:02.280
That came from your phone.

05:02.650 --> 05:05.280
I went ahead and hacked it.

05:05.450 --> 05:08.030
If it's up to me, I can take care
of anything before breakfast.

05:08.030 --> 05:10.450
He's only a first year,
but he's also our treasurer.

05:10.450 --> 05:14.370
He looks like an elementary school student,
but he's a genius hacker, Riro Takumi!

05:13.750 --> 05:15.040
GENIUS HACKER
RIRO TAKUMI

05:14.370 --> 05:15.540
Trope!

05:15.540 --> 05:17.420
They went with this direction
for the genius type, huh?

05:17.710 --> 05:20.040
And now, checkmate!

05:20.040 --> 05:21.960
Slamming the enter key is so cliché!

05:23.760 --> 05:26.130
Our PR Officer.
Leave the fighting to him.

05:26.130 --> 05:28.720
The giant, beastly musclehead, Burst!

05:28.140 --> 05:30.720
GIANT BEASTLY MUSCLEHEAD
BURST

05:28.720 --> 05:30.720
Enough already!
How many are there?

05:30.930 --> 05:34.350
Hey, can I kill this guy?

05:34.600 --> 05:39.310
For General Affairs, we have the crazy,
murderous psychopath who loves licking knives,

05:39.730 --> 05:40.650
Kyoki Saiko!

05:39.730 --> 05:42.860
PSYCHOPATH WHO LOVES
LICKING KNIVES
KYOKI SAIKO

05:40.650 --> 05:42.860
Psychopath who loves licking knives?

05:43.190 --> 05:46.860
Program complete.
Initiating mission.

05:47.070 --> 05:51.120
Our other General Affairs, the very eccentric
and unidentified mysterious robot,

05:51.120 --> 05:52.950
Daiki Sakai Mark II.

05:51.120 --> 05:56.370
MYSTERIOUS ROBOT
DAIKI SAKAI MARK II

05:52.950 --> 05:56.370
A what? Is this a trope?
I don't know anymore!

05:56.540 --> 05:57.670
Stop it already!

05:57.670 --> 06:00.250
Are you the damn Avengers?
What am I even seeing here?

06:00.750 --> 06:02.880
You're just making up
your own characters, aren't you?

06:03.050 --> 06:05.460
Just take a long, hard look at yourselves.

06:05.460 --> 06:08.340
Can you even properly do
Student Council work like that?

06:10.680 --> 06:12.470
Doesn't seem like it.

06:12.810 --> 06:15.980
These idiots can't enforce
any rules on us. Come on, Nico.

06:16.350 --> 06:19.150
I will not allow such insolence
in the presence of the Student Council!

06:19.150 --> 06:21.480
I'll just carve the lesson onto your body!

06:35.830 --> 06:37.870
This guy is strong.

06:38.040 --> 06:39.710
You're the ones who are weak.

06:39.960 --> 06:41.960
Please do not be so wroth with them.

06:53.100 --> 06:55.350
Allow me to apologize for my subordinates.

06:59.230 --> 07:03.020
He's descending down the stairs like someone
from Takarazuka. Kind of irritating.

07:03.400 --> 07:06.190
I am the Student Council President,
Tenryu Kiyomiya.

07:06.480 --> 07:08.150
Wait, Kiyomiya?

07:08.320 --> 07:10.530
I think he's Suzuka Kiyomiya's
older brother.

07:10.530 --> 07:12.660
Oh, her older brother?

07:12.660 --> 07:15.700
Thank you for taking care
of my sister the other day.

07:15.950 --> 07:17.540
Allow me to express my gratitude.

07:17.830 --> 07:20.330
Nico Wakatsuki and Morihito Otogi.

07:20.710 --> 07:23.670
You seem
like a reasonable person, President.

07:24.040 --> 07:26.750
Why do you wish to oppress
the magic that saved your sister?

07:26.960 --> 07:29.720
Nico works hard every day
to help the students in this school.

07:31.970 --> 07:34.050
Nico was born as a witch.

07:34.050 --> 07:36.970
Isn't it discrimination to be against
a trait that someone was born with?

07:38.310 --> 07:40.480
- Look how you've grown.
- We just met.

07:40.730 --> 07:42.850
Please do not be so wroth with them.

07:42.850 --> 07:44.730
Is your vocabulary limited?

07:44.730 --> 07:46.980
And what's with that hand?
Can you stop that?

07:47.230 --> 07:49.940
Move your hand!
Is it stuck to your hat or something?

07:50.440 --> 07:54.370
My hand is stuck to my hat, you see.

07:54.370 --> 07:56.580
Your hand is stuck on your hat, huh?

07:56.580 --> 07:57.870
How is that possible?

07:57.870 --> 07:59.040
Begin explanation.

07:59.040 --> 08:03.870
It is the same phenomenon where Jotaro's hat
and his hair have combined together.

08:03.870 --> 08:06.130
That didn't explain anything. Can it, robot.

08:06.340 --> 08:09.130
This year's first years
sure are a spirited bunch.

08:09.260 --> 08:10.760
I just want to eat them up.

08:10.880 --> 08:11.880
Checkmate.

08:12.130 --> 08:14.390
Let the hell show begin!

08:14.510 --> 08:16.260
Everyone, just shut up!

08:17.890 --> 08:19.470
I said shut up!

08:19.470 --> 08:23.640
Moi is surrounded by the type of people
he doesn't like, so he's just purely raging.

08:23.890 --> 08:25.600
Please do not be so wroth with them.

08:25.600 --> 08:26.650
Huh?!

08:27.060 --> 08:29.780
My apologies,
please forgive me for my mistake.

08:30.230 --> 08:35.320
Regarding Nico Wakatsuki's magic, there's been
a discussion among the Student Council.

08:35.740 --> 08:39.160
I'm inclined to approve it,
given it was used to help my sister.

08:39.540 --> 08:41.660
But there's been a resistance
within my subordinates.

08:42.120 --> 08:47.040
They want to help the students and gain fame,
but there seems to be a witch in the way.

08:47.210 --> 08:48.630
So you guys are just jealous?

08:48.750 --> 08:52.300
All right. I shall once again re-examine
the case regarding Wakatsuki's magic.

08:52.300 --> 08:54.590
Are you guilt tripping me
because of jealousy?

08:54.880 --> 08:56.260
There's one condition.

08:56.260 --> 08:58.140
I said don't guilt trip me.

08:58.140 --> 08:59.760
The way you moved your body...

09:00.260 --> 09:04.770
Your loyalty to Wakatsuki for wanting
to protect her, and that cool-headedness...

09:05.190 --> 09:06.690
It's absolutely ideal.

09:08.610 --> 09:10.320
Join the Student Council, Otogi!

09:10.320 --> 09:12.150
This is a really weird plot twist!

09:12.400 --> 09:13.990
How does your brain even get to that?

09:13.990 --> 09:18.950
Otogi, what do you think is missing
from the current Student Council?

09:19.240 --> 09:20.660
- Common sense?
- Wrong!

09:21.330 --> 09:25.160
The missing piece to this puzzle
is a cool-type obedient fighting character...

09:25.620 --> 09:26.960
In other words, you!

09:26.620 --> 09:29.420
COOL-TYPE FIGHTING GUY
MORIHITO OTOGI

09:26.960 --> 09:29.420
Don't talk to me like I'm some kind of trope!

09:29.840 --> 09:32.420
And now, I could have
my Student Council Ten.

09:32.420 --> 09:36.380
And the best part is that
he's the descendant of an ogre.

09:38.180 --> 09:40.010
I want you, Otogi!

09:40.640 --> 09:43.140
This person's character is into weird things.

09:43.140 --> 09:44.640
Let's just get going.

09:45.310 --> 09:48.400
Wait! Our conversation is not over.
Everyone, after him!

09:48.520 --> 09:51.070
That first year sure doesn't listen.

09:51.070 --> 09:52.900
Those two are so adorable.

09:53.070 --> 09:55.320
Hmph, what's even good about him, anyway?

09:55.320 --> 09:57.360
I hear the wailing of an ogre.

09:57.360 --> 09:59.240
Let me murder him!

09:59.240 --> 10:01.080
It'll be easy if we track them.

10:01.080 --> 10:03.290
Understood, beginning mission.

10:04.040 --> 10:07.410
No way am I ever joining a group like that.

10:15.880 --> 10:18.130
Kan, over here!

10:20.180 --> 10:21.850
Thanks for bringing our bags.

10:22.180 --> 10:24.180
Why are you here on the rooftop?

10:24.560 --> 10:27.390
For some reason, the Student Council
President took a liking to me.

10:27.770 --> 10:32.150
We've been running and hiding, but when
we got here, we couldn't really go anywhere.

10:32.150 --> 10:35.030
It's fine, isn't it? Why don't you
join the Student Council?

10:35.030 --> 10:38.650
And then become president next year
so you could make my tuition free.

10:38.650 --> 10:41.660
Your misunderstanding of what
the Student Council does is super obvious.

10:41.660 --> 10:43.450
The Student Council members, huh?

10:43.740 --> 10:47.000
There was an introduction video
of them on the school's website.

10:47.000 --> 10:50.250
Yeah? It says it's a close coverage video
of the Student Council's activities.

10:50.250 --> 10:52.040
Let's all watch it.

10:52.040 --> 10:53.840
I don't know if I want to.

10:53.090 --> 10:55.090
STUDENT COUNCIL ACTIVITIES
~ CLOSE ENCOUNTER WITH THE LEADERSHIP ~

10:55.710 --> 10:57.010
Whoa, that scared me!

10:57.880 --> 10:59.550
It looks like they went all out.

10:59.720 --> 11:01.390
Somehow this kind of thing irritates me.

11:02.090 --> 11:03.680
Why are the words in vertical lines?

11:03.680 --> 11:06.810
If the words also flow vertically,
then no one can read them!

11:07.060 --> 11:09.770
Oh no, it's already over.
I was only able to read one line.

11:09.770 --> 11:11.600
Is the person who made this an idiot?

11:12.650 --> 11:16.860
<i>Once classes are over, the officers will slowly
gather in the Student Council Meeting Room.</i>

11:17.030 --> 11:18.740
And then it begins all normally?

11:18.740 --> 11:21.110
What the heck was that useless opening?

11:21.660 --> 11:23.120
Heyo.

11:21.660 --> 11:23.120
STUDENT COUNCIL VICE PRESIDENT
SECOND YEAR IBARA IBU

11:23.450 --> 11:25.030
So tired.

11:25.030 --> 11:28.580
What the hell is she wearing? Am I seeing
this right? Her boobs are all over the place.

11:28.580 --> 11:31.830
She's wearing her uniform way too casually
for a Student Council member.

11:32.040 --> 11:33.830
There are eight more of those.

11:33.830 --> 11:34.710
What?

11:35.000 --> 11:38.550
There's a camera today?
Go easy on me, okay?

11:35.000 --> 11:42.930
THE OTHER VICE PRESIDENT
SECOND YEAR YUZURU KENMOCHI

11:38.550 --> 11:40.970
This guy is way too shady right off the bat.

11:40.970 --> 11:44.470
His Kansai accent intonation
also sounds kinda shady, too.

11:56.820 --> 11:58.650
Nothing, after all that?

11:58.650 --> 12:01.570
You just pretend to say
something meaningful, but then don't?

12:01.570 --> 12:04.110
He's just emitting
strong character vibes and that's it.

12:04.450 --> 12:08.870
GENERAL AFFAIRS
SECOND YEAR
KYOKI SAIKO

12:04.990 --> 12:06.240
Nope, nope, nope!

12:06.240 --> 12:08.870
This one's definitely crazy.
Just look at his name!

12:09.080 --> 12:11.870
<i>He's the most dangerous man
in the Student Council.</i>

12:12.120 --> 12:15.830
Could that be our classmate
Tosaku Saiko's older brother?

12:15.830 --> 12:17.130
Looks like he is.

12:21.010 --> 12:22.630
He just cut his tongue!

12:22.800 --> 12:24.800
Why are you even licking a knife?
Are you an idiot?

12:24.800 --> 12:26.850
It's so dangerous that I can't watch.

12:26.850 --> 12:29.010
That's what they meant by dangerous man?

12:29.270 --> 12:32.520
Hey Riro, what're you working on?

12:32.850 --> 12:36.020
<i>Our first year treasurer,
Riro Takumi, is a hacker.</i>

12:33.100 --> 12:36.020
TREASURER
FIRST YEAR
RIRO TAKUMI

12:36.560 --> 12:39.530
I'm hacking into Shonen Magazine's
Editing Department!

12:39.530 --> 12:40.900
Really, what the hell are you doing?

12:41.110 --> 12:41.990
I got in!

12:41.990 --> 12:43.320
He got in?

12:43.320 --> 12:46.660
The password was
"hashtag-noway100volumes."

12:46.660 --> 12:48.280
That's kind of an old joke.

12:48.280 --> 12:51.290
GENERAL AFFAIRS
SECOND YEAR
DAICHI SAKAI MARK II

12:48.490 --> 12:49.660
Excellent work, everyone.

12:49.660 --> 12:51.290
Who the hell is that?

12:51.580 --> 12:53.250
This person is a robot.

12:53.250 --> 12:55.790
What do you mean a robot?
What's going on in his head?

12:56.540 --> 12:58.420
<i>This man is not entirely a robot.</i>

12:58.420 --> 13:00.000
He's saying he's not a robot.

13:00.340 --> 13:02.760
<i>If anything, he's closer to a cyborg.</i>

13:02.760 --> 13:04.800
I see, a union of person and machine.

13:05.340 --> 13:06.180
<i>It's cardboard.</i>

13:06.180 --> 13:07.550
Then that's a person!

13:07.850 --> 13:10.560
What do you mean a cardboard box
that's close to a cyborg?

13:10.560 --> 13:11.930
At least he sounds like a robot.

13:11.930 --> 13:14.230
I'm wondering about
the craftmanship for Mark I.

13:15.520 --> 13:19.360
Head component destruction level one.
Commence repairs with tape.

13:19.360 --> 13:21.570
How does it feel to talk
from inside that thing?

13:23.650 --> 13:26.070
STUDENT COUNCIL PRESIDENT
THIRD YEAR
TENRYU KIYOMIYA

13:30.830 --> 13:34.250
The atmosphere changed.
So this is the Student Council President.

13:37.580 --> 13:40.290
<i>When I look at him, I feel uneasy.</i>

13:40.670 --> 13:44.670
<i>Within all that charisma, why do I feel
a strange sense of closeness?</i>

13:45.260 --> 13:46.590
Are there any reports?

13:47.840 --> 13:49.350
Go ahead, Kuromitsu.

13:49.600 --> 13:51.180
Her aura is so dark.

13:49.930 --> 13:55.850
SECRETARY
FIRST YEAR
KUROMITSU AMAI

13:51.180 --> 13:53.890
President's atmosphere
has already been overwritten.

13:53.890 --> 13:58.020
Melting together in a muddy manner,
and then birthed in this cursed world.

13:58.020 --> 14:03.360
Even after being burned with a white, powdery
hellfire, the seashell's mouth remaineth closed.

14:04.820 --> 14:07.110
Syrup, what madness is she spouting?

14:07.490 --> 14:09.870
We baked madeleines for snack time.

14:07.740 --> 14:11.620
SECRETARY
FIRST YEAR
SYRUP AMAI

14:09.870 --> 14:11.620
A recipe for madeleines.

14:11.870 --> 14:15.750
So she just baked some sweets?
What was that dark atmosphere just now?

14:15.870 --> 14:19.630
<i>This is the other secretary, Syrup,
and she's Kuromitsu's older twin.</i>

14:19.960 --> 14:22.750
Wonderful.
Let us all partake and continue on.

14:22.880 --> 14:24.260
Okay!

14:24.260 --> 14:26.010
Looks like they're having tons of fun!

14:26.840 --> 14:28.630
I have something, too.

14:27.630 --> 14:30.010
PR OFFICER
SECOND YEAR
BURST (ASUTO ISHIBA)

14:28.630 --> 14:30.010
Go ahead, Burst.

14:30.140 --> 14:33.140
Lately, I've been seeing students
not properly wearing their uniforms.

14:33.140 --> 14:34.720
Are you one to talk?

14:34.720 --> 14:39.140
I had a discussion
with the guidance counselor about it, too.

14:39.140 --> 14:42.150
<i>Our Public Relations Officer,
Burst, is such a hard worker.</i>

14:45.360 --> 14:48.740
Now they're all talking
about the uniform issue.

14:48.740 --> 14:51.160
That's because they're not even
wearing theirs properly.

14:51.620 --> 14:55.410
I'm aiming for a school where students
can let their individuality shine.

14:55.580 --> 14:58.790
I've been submitting paperwork
and having discussions with the teachers

14:58.790 --> 15:02.420
requesting that students be allowed to wear
their uniforms in the manner they see fit.

15:02.630 --> 15:04.340
Let me take on this issue.

15:04.340 --> 15:06.550
Wow, President is a pretty cool guy.

15:06.550 --> 15:09.590
This guy doesn't even retain
the base structure of our uniform.

15:09.680 --> 15:10.930
Is there anything else?

15:11.140 --> 15:15.060
I gathered the sports club reports,
but I don't know what to do with them.

15:15.310 --> 15:17.180
It's fine, I'll take care of it.

15:17.180 --> 15:19.690
I bricked my laptop
and all the budget data went with it.

15:19.940 --> 15:22.690
I still have them on these documents,
so I'll fix it.

15:22.900 --> 15:24.400
Foul meeting minutes.

15:24.400 --> 15:25.270
I'll record them.

15:25.480 --> 15:27.780
The supplies shelf is very unorganized.

15:27.780 --> 15:29.400
Just leave it there, please.

15:30.860 --> 15:33.910
What's going on?
President took on everyone's work.

15:33.910 --> 15:37.870
President has quietly started working hard,
and the rest of the members are having a party.

15:37.870 --> 15:39.660
That's really sad!

15:40.160 --> 15:42.920
<i>Surrounded by no-gooders and
having to clean up after their mess...</i>

15:43.750 --> 15:44.790
<i>This is...</i>

15:45.340 --> 15:46.880
<i>me!</i>

15:48.590 --> 15:49.800
I'm relating to him super hard!

15:50.130 --> 15:52.050
A-Are you okay, Otogi?

15:52.050 --> 15:55.760
I feel like I can completely understand
President and it hurts my head!

15:55.760 --> 15:57.310
He's gone off the rails.

15:58.100 --> 16:00.060
Tenryu, aren't you just the nicest person.

16:01.100 --> 16:04.060
It's just that I cherish
each and every one of you.

16:04.520 --> 16:06.020
President.

16:06.320 --> 16:08.320
KINGSHIP

16:06.820 --> 16:07.860
Kingship.

16:08.730 --> 16:11.900
I was taught kingcraft ever since I was a child.

16:12.450 --> 16:14.320
So that I can pursue the path of a king.

16:15.280 --> 16:16.200
Kingship.

16:16.910 --> 16:17.910
Kingship.

16:18.830 --> 16:21.410
And then, that's all I thought about.

16:21.910 --> 16:23.500
Maybe it's because of that,

16:24.540 --> 16:28.590
but in fictional tales, I can only like characters
who are pursuing their road to kingship.

16:28.590 --> 16:30.460
That's kind of a weird reason, right?

16:30.970 --> 16:34.800
Just watching everyone's kingship
puts me at great ease.

16:34.930 --> 16:36.550
Please continue to be by my side.

16:36.550 --> 16:38.680
- President.
- Oh, President.

16:38.680 --> 16:42.940
<i>Now I understand the reason
why I can't come to hate this guy.</i>

16:43.520 --> 16:46.860
But I also don't want
to be liked by him.

16:47.060 --> 16:50.940
I feel so bad for Moi
getting anxiety over a strange issue.

16:51.030 --> 16:53.490
There you are, Otogi!

16:53.700 --> 16:54.610
President?

16:54.610 --> 16:57.120
I will have Otogi join the Student Council!

16:57.530 --> 16:59.870
However, I don't like forcing people.

16:59.950 --> 17:04.080
I'm going to challenge you, and if you lose,
you must join the Student Council.

17:04.080 --> 17:05.370
So you are forcing me!

17:05.880 --> 17:08.540
You won't know when and where I attack you
within the school grounds.

17:08.540 --> 17:11.420
If I strike you even once, I win. Got it?

17:11.420 --> 17:13.760
The rules are getting more unreasonable.

17:13.970 --> 17:17.010
Do not resist!
Join the Student Council, Otogi!

17:17.010 --> 17:21.720
No way. I'm already
sick of the Student Council.

17:21.720 --> 17:26.440
Oh, dear. And so, Moi and President's chases
will continue to happen.

17:26.440 --> 17:28.940
Don't say it like it's gonna be a trope!

17:38.950 --> 17:41.830
OTOGI

17:52.510 --> 17:53.960
<i>I can't do it!</i>

17:54.170 --> 17:59.010
<i>Wait, would it be rude to suddenly
come over unannounced on the weekend?</i>

17:54.590 --> 18:01.260
A STRAY CAT'S BUBBLE OF BLISS

17:59.010 --> 18:02.720
<i>I might seem like a stalker
since I know their address, too.</i>

18:03.140 --> 18:04.310
<i>Yeah, I can't do this.</i>

18:04.310 --> 18:07.390
<i>If I think about it, there's a witch and
a tengu also living in the house,</i>

18:07.390 --> 18:10.610
<i>so it's not like I'll get a chance
to speak to him alone.</i>

18:10.820 --> 18:12.230
<i>This isn't looking good.</i>

18:12.440 --> 18:14.740
<i>Yep, I'm gonna give up for today.</i>

18:14.740 --> 18:17.400
<i>There are way too many reasons
why I shouldn't.</i>

18:21.080 --> 18:22.740
<i>Morihito Otogi!</i>

18:22.910 --> 18:27.460
<i>He's by himself! A-A beautiful chance
has suddenly presented itself.</i>

18:34.210 --> 18:35.970
<i>Nemu, you big dummy!</i>

18:36.170 --> 18:40.260
Hey, you're that cat from before.
Back again, huh?

18:40.260 --> 18:42.100
<i>Why did I transform?</i>

18:42.470 --> 18:45.100
<i>Because I thought this would be
an easier way to handle it?</i>

18:45.100 --> 18:47.850
<i>Because I want him to pet me again?</i>

18:48.230 --> 18:49.480
Would you like to come inside?

18:50.600 --> 18:53.980
<i>I guess I just fall easily
to these kinds of things.</i>

18:54.980 --> 18:56.070
I'm home.

18:56.070 --> 18:57.360
<i>Pardon the intrusion.</i>

18:57.490 --> 18:59.490
Stray cats! So funny!

19:00.610 --> 19:03.330
Stray Cat comedy is too funny!

19:03.330 --> 19:07.370
<i>Oh the manzai duo?
Ugh, that really scared me.</i>

19:09.170 --> 19:10.750
<i>He's laughing pretty hard.</i>

19:11.250 --> 19:12.960
Did Skate Dandy come out yet?

19:12.960 --> 19:14.250
They're coming out later.

19:14.250 --> 19:16.510
Morihito, you really like
Sket-Dan a lot, huh?

19:16.760 --> 19:20.630
<i>Everyone's just hanging out on the weekend
together, and laughing at comedy shows?</i>

19:20.630 --> 19:23.220
<i>What kind of fun lifestyle is this?</i>

19:23.220 --> 19:25.760
That's right, the cat from before
is here again.

19:25.970 --> 19:28.520
Oh, kitty cat! You're here!

19:28.810 --> 19:30.270
Do you like this place after all?

19:30.270 --> 19:32.020
<i>Oh no, please don't get too excited!</i>

19:34.610 --> 19:39.280
Uh oh. I'm so sorry, I spilled my honey
Calpico ramune drink on you.

19:40.570 --> 19:43.660
<i>Ugh, what is this sticky-sweet liquid?</i>

19:46.040 --> 19:47.950
You've gotten all sticky.

19:50.580 --> 19:52.080
Okay, come here, please.

19:52.080 --> 19:55.420
<i>How is it possible that a situation worse
than getting pet has presented itself to me?!</i>

19:55.670 --> 19:59.800
I know you might not like getting wet,
but we should really wash that off of you.

19:59.800 --> 20:00.970
<i>I cannot possibly do that.</i>

20:00.970 --> 20:03.930
<i>I don't know what's going on,
but this has a very dubious feel to it!</i>

20:04.220 --> 20:06.180
What's wrong? Don't be shy.

20:06.180 --> 20:08.930
<i>You don't even know how I feel,
so please stop sounding like a boyfriend!</i>

20:09.140 --> 20:10.680
Come on, the water's just fine.

20:11.190 --> 20:15.190
<i>Oh but, my body is remembering...</i>

20:15.400 --> 20:17.440
<i>how it felt when those hands
touched me.</i>

20:17.440 --> 20:20.400
I don't have a sponge.
Guess I'll wash with my hand.

20:20.820 --> 20:22.700
<i>Pardon the intrusion.</i>

20:26.830 --> 20:28.200
Hope the water's not too hot.

20:28.950 --> 20:31.210
<i>It's the best.</i>

20:35.500 --> 20:36.750
And now for the bubbles...

20:40.170 --> 20:41.220
<i>Ba-bump.</i>

20:44.300 --> 20:47.180
<i>A dress made from bubbles.
By Nemu Miyao.</i>

20:48.600 --> 20:52.730
<i>I love soap, ribbons,
and small paperback books.</i>

20:52.730 --> 20:56.730
<i>In the bathroom,
I've become Cinderella in a white dress.</i>

20:56.730 --> 21:00.860
<i>When the clock strikes, these bubbles
will disappear like it was just a dream.</i>

21:00.860 --> 21:02.320
<i>They're bubbles after all.</i>

21:03.570 --> 21:05.320
<i>Oh no, could this be...</i>

21:05.990 --> 21:09.330
<i>Nemu Miyao's shapeshifting magic
will turn her back if she falls asleep.</i>

21:09.740 --> 21:13.500
<i>I really cannot fall asleep here.
If I do...</i>

21:14.250 --> 21:16.420
<i>It'll be the most dubious situation ever</i>

21:16.420 --> 21:19.630
<i>if a girl covered in bubbles
suddenly appears in the bathroom.</i>

21:19.800 --> 21:22.510
<i>Oh but the little sandmen
have come to greet me.</i>

21:23.050 --> 21:25.090
<i>But no! I'll be fine today!</i>

21:25.090 --> 21:28.760
<i>I've learned my lesson from before,
and I have the iron will to not fall asleep!</i>

21:32.730 --> 21:34.770
<i>Oh no, I'm going to fall asleep.</i>

21:35.230 --> 21:37.270
<i>This is just way too comfortable.</i>

21:37.270 --> 21:39.440
<i>After getting a scrub-scrub
from an ogre's hands</i>

21:39.440 --> 21:42.190
<i>and then get brushed with warm wind,
you'd fall asleep.</i>

21:42.990 --> 21:45.240
<i>What a heavenly, spring breeze.</i>

21:45.650 --> 21:51.950
<i>It's like riding behind your boyfriend's
motorcycle in the summer.</i>

21:55.620 --> 21:56.540
<i>I fell asleep?</i>

21:57.750 --> 21:59.790
<i>It's over!</i>

22:06.050 --> 22:08.300
Skate Dandy is so funny!

22:08.300 --> 22:10.050
<i>Sket-Dan to the rescue!</i>

22:10.510 --> 22:12.310
<i>He's laughing so much!</i>

22:13.810 --> 22:16.690
<i>Tiptoe. Tiptoe.</i>

22:21.320 --> 22:23.150
What am I even doing?

22:24.150 --> 22:29.450
I really want to stop sneaking in, experience
a blissful moment, and then regret it afterwards.

22:30.620 --> 22:33.910
I wonder if there'll be a day
when I can finally come forward.

22:35.160 --> 22:37.250
Wait, where am I?

22:41.290 --> 22:42.840
<i>This feeling...</i>

22:43.380 --> 22:44.590
<i>Alert!</i>

22:47.300 --> 22:48.470
<i>That means...</i>

22:49.300 --> 22:50.850
<i>there's a warlock nearby?</i>

23:10.110 --> 23:12.490
<i>Is that the warlock? No...</i>

23:12.490 --> 23:14.870
So what are the results?

23:14.870 --> 23:17.450
How many do we have?

23:17.660 --> 23:18.620
<i>She's further back.</i>

23:18.870 --> 23:22.210
Forty... No, around fifty people.

23:24.170 --> 23:29.180
A good amount. We begin
as soon as preparations are complete.

23:30.550 --> 23:34.510
Capture Nico Wakatsuki.

23:39.230 --> 23:41.900
<i>A warlock is after Nico Wakatsuki!</i>

23:49.450 --> 23:51.570
<i>I have to warn her!</i>

23:57.540 --> 24:01.080
Hey! I'm Tenryu.
That Otogi guy is really strong.

24:01.080 --> 24:03.580
- We will fight alongside you.
- We won't let you fight him alone.

24:01.920 --> 24:03.580
Come on, let's go!

24:03.580 --> 24:06.130
Next time on WITCHWATCH Z,
defeat Morihito!

24:06.130 --> 24:08.920
The Student Council's
greatest kamehame...

24:06.130 --> 24:11.970
NEXT EPISODE
DOGS AND RAINDROPS, PART 1

24:08.920 --> 24:10.170
HAAA!!

24:10.170 --> 24:11.970
You need to be disciplined.
